W2  no local EOS mu(rho, T_perp, r, rho_b) has the target as its static equilibrium
==============================================================================================================
    equilibrium mu' + g_tot = 0 with mu_tau = 0 (rho_b' is an independent profile function):
      coefficient of rho_b*u : 4*pi*G*(T*mu_T + mu_rho*rho)/T
      coefficient of rho_b   : -16*pi**2*G**2*mu_rho*rho**2/(T*a0)
      => {mu_T: 0, mu_rho: 0}
      remaining equation gives mu_r = -T*a0/(4*pi*G*rho)   (must equal d mu/dr at fixed rho, T, with mu_rho = mu_T = 0 ->  mu = mu(r) only)
      integrability: d(mu_r)/d rho = T*a0/(4*pi*G*rho**2)  vs  d(mu_rho)/dr = 0
  [PASS] W2 (sympy) no equation of state whose energy depends on x through LOCAL fields of Phi_b (T_perp, g_N ~ r T, rho_b) can have the target as its static equilibrium on generic baryon profiles: the coefficients of rho_b force mu_rho = mu_T = 0, then mu_r = -a0 T/(4 pi G rho) is inconsistent
         mu_rho = 0, mu_T = 0, mu_r = -T*a0/(4*pi*G*rho), d mu_r/d rho = T*a0/(4*pi*G*rho**2) != 0

